  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>AB</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are diatomic molecules. If the bond enthalpies of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> are in the ratio<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the bond enthalpy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_________kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "800",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>First write balanced reaction for the formation of one mole of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math>&nbsp;with the help of diatomic molecule:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>AB</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi>reaction</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi>AB</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>let</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi>AB</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p>Bond enthalpy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
